              "id": "CVE-2025-53864",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "com.nimbusds/nimbus-jose-jwt: Uncontrolled recursion in Connect2id Nimbus JOSE + JWT"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Connect2id Nimbus JOSE + JWT 10.0.x before 10.0.2 and 9.37.x before 9.37.4 allows a remote attacker to cause a denial of service via a deeply nested JSON object supplied in a JWT claim set, because of uncontrolled recursion. NOTE: this is independent of the Gson 2.11.0 issue because the Connect2id product could have checked the JSON object nesting depth, regardless of what limits (if any) were imposed by Gson."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-53864",
